      "content": "The responsive check never measures the readout or its values, so it can pass when Banked/Result at the Stop text is clipped inside a width-constrained container. `expectNoSidewaysScroll` only checks document scrollWidth and will also pass if an ancestor hides that overflow. Include the readout values in the horizontal-fit checks and verify they are not clipped (for example, using the existing `expectShownInFull` helper), so fixing page overflow by hiding content cannot silently satisfy B9.5.",
